course: dictionary
lesson: 10014
title: Temporary: just for now
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Temporary means lasting for only a short time, not forever. Something temporary is there for now, and it will be taken away or changed later. The opposite is permanent, which means it lasts for ever.
explain: «Temporary traffic lights at roadworks take turns letting one direction of traffic through a single lane.» The clue is at roadworks. Roadworks end, so the lights will be taken away when the work is done. Temporary tells you they are not meant to stay.
explain: «Scaffolding is a temporary frame of steel poles and boards.» Builders put scaffolding up to help them work, then take it down. A quick check: swap in "for now" for temporary. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Temporary means lasting only for a short time, not forever.
fact: Permanent is the opposite of temporary.
fact: Temporary can also mean used for a while until something permanent is ready.
fact: A «temporary tattoo» lasts only a short time, then fades away.
fact: In science, melting ice is a temporary change, because it can freeze back again.
exercise: «Temporary traffic lights at roadworks take turns letting one direction of traffic through.» What does temporary mean? | Made of steel | *Lasting only for a short time | Very bright and shiny | Lasting forever
exercise: «Scaffolding is a temporary frame of steel poles and boards.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the frame is not meant to stay forever. | steel | *temporary | boards | scaffolding
exercise: Which phrase describes a job that lasts only for now? | *A temporary job | A huge wall | A permanent home | A lasting smile
test: Which word is the opposite of temporary? | loud | quick | *permanent | cheap
test: In science, which is a temporary change? | Breaking an egg | *Melting ice | Cutting a piece of wood
exam: What does a temporary teacher mean? | A teacher who teaches only maths | A teacher who is very old | A teacher who will stay for life | *A teacher who covers for a while, not forever
